  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14159351/assets/05b54d1b8e401f49861e335fd4736566441017576b30d9b56a6bdfe5e670bffb.png)\n\nWhich of the following intervals corresponds to the segment shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nThe given interval can be represented by the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-3\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,2\n$$\n\nWe can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\in (-3,2)\n$$",
